messages:
maria: Heads up — customer hit parse error when following the Node streaming example for /v1/generate-stream. Docs show JSON chunks but server emits SSE (text/event-stream). Error: SyntaxError: Unexpected token d at JSON.parse.

kevin: Can you paste the snippet path and error? I'll reproduce locally.

maria: Snippet: docs/snippets/node/generate-stream.md. Error from Dedicated customer.

sam: Quick patch for Node: ```js
stream.on('data', chunk => {
  const s = chunk.toString()
  s.split(/\r?\n/).forEach(line => {
    if (!line.startsWith('data:')) return
    const obj = JSON.parse(line.replace(/^data:\s*/, ''))
    // handle obj
  })
})
``` Add migration blurb: "Streaming returns SSE; parse lines or use sdk.stream helper."

olga: OpenAPI wrongly lists application/json. I'll open a PR to change response content to text/event-stream and update Node/Python snippets + add migration guide.

docs-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/498 — changes: openapi media-type, node+python snippets, migration note. CI: docs-lint passed.

kevin: I'll add an SSE sample vector in runtime tests to validate examples. Ping me for exact payload.

maria: Customer can use helper or non-streaming endpoint as fallback. They want immediate docs workaround.

sam: I'll land the snippet + blurb now and link the PR in the customer's ticket.

olga: I'll follow up with full migration guide in docs/migration/streaming-sse.md and add FAQ entries. ETA EOD.

maria: Thanks — marking resolved unless the customer reopens.
